      "Apple's stock is now down 1% in Monday afternoon trading, after it had been in positive territory for much of the day and for much of the WWDC keynote as well.",
      "Shares turned negative toward the end of the keynote and have continued moving lower. Late in the keynote, Apple acknowledged that it wouldn't be able to roll out its new AI features in all markets right away and that it was looking to find a solution that would allow it to comply with E.U. rules."
